      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(discord): gate guild metadata reads [AI]",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users who configured Discord read allowlists could still have guild-level metadata read through Discord action tools when an arbitrary guild or channel ID was supplied.\n\nAI-assisted change.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Discord guild metadata and thread-list read paths now use the same read-target authorization checks as message reads. Guild-wide metadata reads require the guild to be allowed without narrowing to a single channel, while channel-specific metadata reads continue to authorize the concrete channel target.\n\nThis keeps Discord admin/mutation permission checks unchanged and does not add config, storage, provider, or migration surfaces.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can expect Discord metadata tools to respect the configured read allowlist consistently. Allowed channel reads and guild-wide reads with a wildcard channel allowlist continue to work; non-allowlisted guilds or channels are rejected before the Discord API read runs.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/discord/src/actions/runtime.test.ts` passed: 1 file, 111 tests.\n",
